WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
FL4N: Feed-forward Latent Model for 4D Novel View Synthesis. Title card with the flan logo.

00:03.000 --> 00:08.000
Twelve frames of a monocular video fan out along a camera arc: every frame is a new viewpoint and a new instant.

00:08.000 --> 00:13.000
A view by time grid. Only the diagonal is observed. A target cell off the diagonal is rendered by FL4N.

00:13.000 --> 00:19.000
Ground truth next to four Gaussian-based baselines showing ghosting, blur, floaters and holes; FL4N's render appears with a check.

00:19.000 --> 00:24.000
Context frames enter a frozen static encoder and become a static latent that knows where to render, not when.

00:24.000 --> 00:30.000
A trainable dynamic encoder with learnable time tokens sits above the frozen static encoder; static injection feeds it; it outputs a residual latent and a dynamic mask.

00:30.000 --> 00:36.000
The residual latent passes a time module, is added to the static latent, and the frozen renderer decodes it. A time slider plays a novel-view video, then a view slider sweeps cameras at a fixed instant.

00:36.000 --> 00:40.000
Three loss cards: RGB, dynamic and mask. Depth, optical flow, 3D motion labels and per-scene optimisation are struck out.

00:40.000 --> 00:45.000
Bar charts of cross-time view synthesis PSNR on NVIDIA, N3DV and CamxTime; FL4N leads every chart, at 40 FPS.

00:45.000 --> 00:47.000
Closing card: FL4N. Latent 4D, no primitives.
